message: "Please cite this manuscript using the metadata below."
title: "Who Is Cloning My Repositories? An Exploration of 598 Daily Clone Events Across Six Public Repositories From Exactly 8,372 Recorded Clone Events ÷ 14 Days—With 0 Visitors, 0 Views, No Referrals, Stars, Forks, or External Public Discussion for DobeWorks and DEGS at the Original Snapshot"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: "McCoy"
    given-names: "Taylor"
date-released: 2026-10-19
version: 1.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tmccoy678/github-clone-traffic-investigation"
abstract: >-
  A descriptive case study of 8,372 GitHub-counted clone events across six public
  repositories in a 14-day window, with a follow-up regularity analysis,
  same-age-account, subject-matched, and numeric-first variation comparisons,
  October 6 event reconstruction, and read-only review and replacement-cost estimate for
  DobeWorks and DEGS. The evidence
  supports selective scheduled and push-triggered automated collection without
  identifying a particular actor.
